8-B9 is beneficial. So I should avoid discarding any of them. So between the options, the tiles not part of B7-B8-B9 are W7, T1, T6, F2, F3, J3. So among these, which is the best to discard.\n\nIf I discard T1, it's a terminal tile. Keeping terminals can be good for scoring patterns like All Terminals or Chicken Hand. But since I have T7-T8-T9 in a Chi, and T1 and T6, maybe keeping T1 isn't necessary. Discarding T1 might be safe.\n\nSimilarly, T6 is part of the previous player's meld. If I discard T6, since it's the last one, no one can take it. So it's safe.\n\nW7 is a single tile. If I discard it, no one might need it. So it's safe.\n\nF2 is a single tile. Safe.\n\nF3: two in hand. Discarding one might be safe, but if someone takes it for a Pung, it's a loss. But with three left, maybe not.\n\nJ3: similar to F3.\n\nSo between these, maybe playing T1 is the safest. Because it's a terminal, and if I discard it, no one can take it for a Chow (since there's only one left). Also, keeping the B7-B8-B9 intact is better for forming a Chi. So playing T1 would be a good move. Alternatively, T6 is also safe.\n\nBut wait, the hand has T6 as a single tile. If I discard T6, since it's the last one, others can't take it. So it's safe. But T6 is part of the previous player's meld. Maybe they already have it, so no one else needs it.\n\nSo between T1 and T6, which is better. Let's see the unshown counts: T1 has 1 left, T6 has 1 left. Discarding either is safe.\n\nBut in terms of hand structure, keeping T1 as a terminal might be useful for patterns like All Terminals or Chicken Hand. However, since I already have a Chi of T7-T8-T9, and if I discard T1, it's just one terminal. Not sure if it's necessary.\n\nAlternatively, keeping T6 might not be useful. Since it's a middle tile, not a terminal. So discarding T1 might be better.\n\nSo the best options are to play T1 or T6. Between them, playing T1 might be better because it's a terminal, and discarding it doesn't affect the potential